      "name": null,
      "problem": "Which of the following is the equation of a vertical asymptote of the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14267109/assets/e01402141f79b247b05980f7f4e830c112a7dcdc24232a8a4c9beefc1de6f603.png)\n\nThe graph has vertical asymptotes at the points that are not in the domain: \n\n$\\,$ $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…$ \n\nAt each asymptote, the graph tends to $-\\infty $ from the left and $\\infty $ from the right.\n\nOf the given equations, the only one that corresponds to an asymptote of the function is $x=7\\pi .$",
